# machines - Nix distributed build farm configuration
# Format: https://nixos.org/manual/nix/stable/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.html
#
# Each line: [protocol://]user@host system ssh-key max-jobs speed-factor supported-features mandatory-features
# Note: Empty fields use defaults, - means "not specified"

# MEMORY CONSTRAINT: 31GB RAM on Zephyr requires conservative max-jobs
# Rule of thumb: ~6GB per build job max (leaves room for system + AI workloads)
# Zephyr: 31GB RAM / 6GB per job = 5 jobs max, using 4 for safety margin
# Nexus: 46GB RAM / 6GB per job = 7 jobs max, using 6 for safety margin

# Zephyr - K8s control plane + node (32 cores, 31GB RAM)
# CONSERVATIVE maxJobs=4 (~7.5GB per job, leaves 1GB headroom for system + AI)
ssh-ng://j_kro@zephyr x86_64-linux - 4 8 kvm,big-parallel,x86-64-v3 -
# Nexus - K8s storage worker + NFS (24 cores, 46GB RAM)
# CONSERVATIVE maxJobs=6 (~7GB per job, leaves 4GB headroom for NFS)
ssh-ng://j_kro@nexus x86_64-linux - 6 5 big-parallel,x86-64-v3 -

# REMOVED: Forge and Sentry are build CLIENTS only (not servers)
# Only Zephyr (control plane) and Nexus (storage) are build servers
# This prevents build contention with GPU workloads (forge) and monitoring stack (sentry)
